**Related Spec**: specs/491-make-the-sdlc-execute-session-an-opus-supervisor-that-inspects-and-steers-every-worker-stage/

# File: scripts/__tests__/execute-goal.test.mjs
# Generated from: specs/529-track-sdlc-execute-s-queued-issues-with-a-claude-code-goal/requirements.md
Feature: Track /sdlc-execute's queued issues with a Claude Code /goal

  @SCN001
  Scenario: Explicit issue tokens set a goal before supervision starts
    Given an interactive Herdr session on an Opus model runs "/sdlc-execute #41 #42"
    When the goal helper reports issues 41 and 42 and the turn completes
    Then the hooks module runs /goal with a condition naming "#41: MERGED and CLOSED" and "#42: MERGED and CLOSED" and the "/sdlc-execute stopped:" line
    And a supervise call made before that goal is set is refused

  @SCN002
  Scenario: A bare run on an issue branch sets a goal for the branch issue
    Given the current branch is "42-add-goal"
    When "sdlc-execute.mjs goal" runs with no issue tokens
    Then it reports exactly issue 42 with that issue's goal condition

  @SCN003
  Scenario: Delivery of every queued issue meets the goal
    Given an execute run with a goal for issues 41 and 42
    When the controller finishes after delivering both issues
    Then the workflow requires the reply to repeat "#41: MERGED and CLOSED" and "#42: MERGED and CLOSED" verbatim

  @SCN004
  Scenario: A halt ends the goal
    Given an execute run with an active goal
    When the session halts with diagnosis "credential required"
    Then the workflow requires the reply to print "/sdlc-execute stopped: credential required"

  @SCN005
  Scenario: A goal that cannot be set refuses the run
    Given an execute run whose goal helper reported its issues
    When the goal command is unavailable in the session
    Then the session is prompted to print "/sdlc-execute stopped: goal_unavailable: goal command unavailable"
    And every supervise call for that run is refused

  @SCN006
  Scenario: A run that selects nothing sets no goal
    Given "/sdlc-execute" runs bare on a non-issue branch
    When the goal helper runs with no tokens
    Then it prints reasonCode "goal_issues_unresolved" and exits 1, and no goal is set
